If I may, Dan is asking why the unit {lo xanto} cannot be (implicitly)=20
{lo ci xanto}, in which case three elephants would be counted as one=20
counting off by threes. Using a property in zilkancu3 would probably be=20
clearer for that reason. As it stands, some people seem to think that=20
the zilkancu3 unit contains a context-dependent inner quantifier, thus=20
counting of by {xo'e mei}. I don't think that's the intended meaning, so=20
it should be stated clearly that we're dealing with singletons.

